@@ -90,6 +90,10 @@ A tool’s `projectContent` installs execution-prepared content before post-exec
 
 A tool can retain pure `presentCall()` and `presentResult()` methods for Host-local consumers. The built-in Web Client does not consume those values. It selects a renderer through `tool.call.toolview` and derives card props from raw call arguments, result content, failure state, and persisted metadata. The [Client-derived presentation decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-08-23-client-derived-tool-presentation.md) owns this transport split.
 
+Optional source capture records provider identity and observed versions separately from tool content and presentation metadata. A producer calls `exec.captureSource(hint)` after it resolves the actual input; a provider handles `tools/source-capture` and returns only `dsh.event-sources/v1` metadata. `sourceCaptureTimeoutMs` defaults to 5000 milliseconds per capture. Missing providers, malformed metadata, cancellation, and expiry yield `unknown` without changing native execution. Hints may contain process-only input text, while recorded matches contain only declared metadata and bounded UTF16 text references.
+
+`exec.recordSourceOutcome()` synchronously records this execution’s structured process outcome without invoking a provider. The final result keeps captured metadata on failure, and PTC dispatches retain only their own facts. A missing namespace means uncollected; readers never reconstruct it from current files. The metadata adds no model-visible instructions or tokens and does not establish task completion. See [the recorded metadata](../../../docs/persistence-catalog.md) for its durable fields.
+
