@@ -71,6 +71,8 @@ When the mounted executor confines commands (for example `dsh-bash-sandbox`), a
 
 A composition with no executor provider never activates the tool. Background calls without the job runtime fail with `background jobs unavailable: load @deepseek-ai/dsh-jobs and @deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-jobs`, and `sandbox_permissions` without a sandboxing executor fails with `sandbox_permissions is not available in this composition (no sandboxing executor to escalate)`. `enableRunInBackground: false` removes the parameter and rejects a forced background call at execution time.
 
+Optional source metadata captures the literal command and resolved working directory before execution, while retaining only provider-owned identifiers and necessary target references. The executor separately records structured process outcome: a nonzero exit, signal, timeout, or abort is failed; exit zero is succeeded; background and promoted runs remain unknown at this call’s return. These facts do not change native `isError`, stdout, stderr, or model-visible exit markers, and process success does not mean task completion. Complex shell syntax or an unproved entry must not be inferred from output. See [source capture](../../core/tools/README.md).
